---
/**
 * Phase 3.3 — `/` becomes the landing page.
 *
 * The two tool panels that used to sit in a 2-up grid here have moved to
 * `/speech-to-text` and `/text-to-speech`. This page is now the thing a
 * visitor lands on *before* choosing a tool, so it does the three jobs a
 * landing page exists to do and nothing else:
 *
 *   1. say what this is (the marketing hero, at the full `{spacing.section}`
 *      band — unlike the tool pages, the vertical space here is not wasted,
 *      because what follows is marketing copy, not a working control);
 *   2. let the visitor reach a tool in one click (the two CTAs);
 *   3. say what the thing does beyond those two headlines (the feature grid).
 *
 * DESIGN.md shapes only. The CTAs are `{components.button-primary}` and
 * `{components.button-secondary}`: marketing pills, `rounded.pill` (100px),
 * `0px 14px` padding, `{typography.button-lg}` (16/20), height set by
 * line-height rather than vertical padding. They are pills rather than the
 * 6px-square app controls because this is the one genuinely marketing context
 * on the site — and DESIGN.md's Don'ts is explicit that the two shapes must
 * not be mixed within one context, which is exactly why the header keeps its
 * own `nav-link` pills to itself.
 *
 * Height note: the pills are `h-10` (40px) rather than 44px. DESIGN.md's
 * 44px clear-target claim is made for "marketing pill CTAs" generally, but the
 * real driver there is line-height (20px) plus padding — `0px 14px` horizontal
 * only — which is 20px tall at its literal token values. `h-10` is 40px, the
 * smallest height that still clears the 40px WCAG 2.5.8 minimum and stays
 * visibly a pill rather than a squashed one. Recorded rather than silently
 * rounded up.
 */
import FeatureCard from '../components/FeatureCard.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="GeminiTTS — speech to text, text to speech"
	description="Record speech and get clean structured writing, or turn a document into natural speech. Speech to text with a live transcript, and text to speech with a cost estimate before you pay for it."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="Gemini · speech ⇄ text"
		title="Say it. Write it. Say it back."
		lede="Two tools, one Gemini API key. Record speech and get clean, structured writing — or paste a document and hear it read back. English, বাংলা, हिन्दी, or let it auto-detect."
	>
		{/*
			The two CTAs. `flex-wrap` so they stack rather than overflow at
			320px. Each is `w-fit`-ish (`inline-flex`, not `flex-1`) so a
			wrapped stack still reads as two buttons of their own natural
			width — DESIGN.md's "pill CTAs go full-width" mobile rule is about
			a lone hero CTA, and two full-width slabs would be ambiguous about
			which one is which.
		*/}
		<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
			<a
				href="/speech-to-text"
				class="inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-pill bg-ink px-3.5 text-base leading-5 font-medium text-on-primary hover:opacity-90"
			>
				Speech to text
			</a>
			<a
				href="/text-to-speech"
				class="inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-pill border border-hairline bg-elevated px-3.5 text-base leading-5 font-medium text-ink hover:bg-hairline-soft"
			>
				Text to speech
			</a>
		</div>
	</Hero>

	{/* `id="main"` is the skip link's target, mounted by SiteHeader. */}
	<main id="main" class="container-page flex-1 pb-24">
		{/*
			DESIGN.md "Grid & Container": "Feature sections use 2-up, 3-up, and
			4-up hairline-card grids that collapse toward 1-up on narrow
			widths", and the breakpoint table puts 2-up grids at 768px. The
			columns start at `sm` (640px) rather than `md`/`lg` because these
			cards are short and a 2-up that waits until 1024px leaves both a
			phone and a tablet with a column of one. `items-start` stops the
			taller card stretching its neighbour.
		*/}
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
			<FeatureCard
				eyebrow="Speech → text"
				title="A transcript, not a wall of text"
				body="Interim words stream in live while you talk, then Smart mode cleans the result into structured prose — or Verbatim keeps exactly what you said."
			/>
			<FeatureCard
				eyebrow="Text → speech"
				title="You know the cost before you pay it"
				body="A spoken-character estimate comes back for the exact text you are about to send, and Confirm stays disabled until it does. Text, Markdown, PDF and Word all work."
			/>
			<FeatureCard
				eyebrow="Languages"
				title="English, বাংলা, हिन्दी, or auto"
				body="Pick a language or let it auto-detect per recording. These are also the three scripts the display type is explicitly tuned for."
			/>
			<FeatureCard
				eyebrow="Your key"
				title="The server's key, or your own"
				body="The server key is the default and nothing about the app changes if you stop here. Bring-your-own-key is on the way: your key would go straight to Google from your browser and never reach this server."
			/>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>

